## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design scalable, resilient streaming pipelines on AWS, balancing compute warm-start strategies, data correctness (exactly-once), deployment safety, and observability under real-world load spikes.

## Key Concepts

- Lambda provisioned concurrency
- Kinesis Enhanced Fan-Out
- Idempotent processing and deduplication
- Dead-letter queues (DLQ)
- Canary/Blue-Green deployment with CodeDeploy
- Observability (CloudWatch, X-Ray)
- Data durability in S3 with versioning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-idempotent handler
function handle(record) {
  const id = record.eventSourceARN + ':' + record.sequenceNumber;
  if (cache.has(id)) return;
  // process
  storeRecord(record);
  cache.set(id, true);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement exactly-once semantics across DynamoDB and S3 writes?
- What metrics signal a regression after deployment, and how would you respond?
